%I A401362 #11 Nov 03 2026 13:52:35
%S A401362 18,30,36,42,45,54,60,66,84,90,100,105,108,126,132,135,140,150,156,
%T A401362 162,168,180,196,198,200,204,210,216,220,225,228,231,234,252,260,264,
%U A401362 270,273,276,280,294,300,306,308,312,315,324,330,340,342,350,360,364,378,380,385,390,392,396
%N A401362 Numbers k whose symmetric representation of sigma(k), SRS(k), contains at least one part that is not unimodal.
%C A401362 A part in SRS(n) is described through its sequence of widths (with their lengths) - e.g. widths in A262045, graphics in A237271, lengths in A237593. The width pattern of a part in SRS(n) is the sequence of runs of identical widths replaced by a single occurrence of the width. It is unimodular if the width pattern increases from 1 to a maximum and then decreases back down to 1.
%e A401362 a(1) = 18 and a(3) = 36 are in the sequence since the associated width pattern of both SRS(18) = {39} and SRS(36) = {91} consisting of single parts is {1 2 1 2 1}.
%e A401362 a(5) = 45 is in the sequence since the width pattern of SRS(45) = {23, 32, 23} is {1 0 1 2 1 2 1 2 1 0 1}; the first and last width pattern of width 1 are trivially unimodal, the center width pattern is not.
%t A401362 (* function unimodalQ[ ] is defined in A401361 *)
%t A401362 a401362[b_] := Select[Range[b], Not[ unimodalQ[#]]&]
%t A401362 a401362[400]
%Y A401362 Complement of A401361.
%Y A401362 Cf. A237270, A237271, A237593, A249223, A249351, A262045.
%K A401362 nonn,new
%O A401362 1,1
